  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 138 AM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nIncreased moisture from Edouard will result in scattered showers \nand storms for the Coastal Plains Tuesday afternoon/evening and \nstretching into the day Wednesday. Edouard looks to get stuck over\neast Texas Wednesday-Friday, bringing scattered showers and \nstorms to the Coastal Plains and portions of the northern Hill \nCountry and northern I-35 Corridor. The primary concern with any \nstorms will be downbursts and locally heavy rainfall that could \nlead to localized and minor flooding issues. Heat and increased \nhumidity will continue and highs will easily climb into the upper \n90s to around 100 most days through the remainder of the forecast \nperiod along with heat indices in the 105-110 range through the \nweekend. One positive thing to note is that we may finally break \nfree of persistent ridging by next weekend as the pattern breaks \ndown in favor of a more active easterly mid-level flow regime.",
